  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed as a suru verb ({監禁|かんきん}する) or in the passive ({監禁|かんきん}される). Common in news reports about criminal cases. In legal terminology, {監禁|かんきん}{罪|ざい} refers to the crime of unlawful confinement.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {不法|ふほう}{監禁|かんきん}: unlawful confinement\n- {監禁|かんきん}{罪|ざい}: crime of confinement\n- {監禁|かんきん}{状態|じょうたい}: state of captivity\n- {監禁|かんきん}される: to be confined\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {拘束|こうそく}: restraint, detention (broader; includes physical restraint)\n- {幽閉|ゆうへい}: imprisonment, confinement (literary; often used for historical contexts)",
